   "rdfs:label": "Quantifier shift fallacy",
   "skos:altLabel": [
    "fallacy of every and some",
    "illicit quantifier shift",
    "quantifier switch fallacy"
   ],
   "skos:broader": {
    "@id": "ct:formal-fallacy"
   },
   "skos:definition": "The invalid inference from \"every A stands in relation R to some B\" to \"some single B stands in relation R to every A\", which swaps the order of a universal and an existential quantifier and so turns a weak claim into a much stronger one.",
