   ],
   "skos:broader": {
    "@id": "ct:reasoning"
   },
   "skos:definition": "The family of practices by which the sciences build reliable knowledge of the natural world: systematic observation, experiment, inductive and deductive reasoning, model building and hypothesis testing, checked by a critical community. Philosophers now mostly doubt that a single fixed recipe captures it.",
