   "skos:definition": "The degree to which the origin of a claim (a person, outlet or document) is perceived as competent and willing to tell the truth on the matter at hand, usually analysed as expertise plus trustworthiness; it legitimately bears on how far to rely on testimony, and it measurably shifts how persuasive a message is.",
